  "notes": "Cash basis village. Governmental = General (incl. Library sub-fund, combined in the p5 statement) and Street, Total Governmental Funds column p5. Business-type = Sanitation and Water and Sewer, Total Proprietary Funds column p7; measure cash; no single printed receipts total, so operating 180,485 + nonoperating 12,111 summed. Governmental roll-forward: 481,146 + 301,576 - 411,553 + 130,780 - 160,175 + 300 (sale of assets) = 342,074. Business: 63,836 + 192,596 - 221,535 + 29,395 = 64,292. Statement Local 75,747 split by the Statement of Activities (fees 59,900 + operating grants 1,595 + miscellaneous 14,252 = 75,747). Balance sheet: governmental from the p4 governmental funds statement (total 342,074 equals p1 governmental column), business-type from p6; combined totals 406,366 from p1. Detail: p9-10 by-fund schedule (actual only) recorded per fund, zero lines omitted; the p8 All Funds budgetary comparison (combined funds) is not recorded to avoid double counting. The p9 schedule's General+Library Local (74,152 + 1,601 = 75,753) and interest (786) differ by 6 from the p5 statement (Local 75,747, interest 792), a classification difference only (sums agree). Transfer cross-check: General out 167,023 includes 6,848 to Library (internal, eliminated on p5: 167,023 - 6,848 = 160,175); 160,175 = 130,165 to Street + 30,010 to Water and Sewer; Sanitation 615 to General. No hidden transfers. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
